@page "/RunOnDocker"

@inherits InstructionsRunOnDockerPageBase
<br />
<MudText Typo="Typo.h5">Step 1 Install Docker on the Raspberry pi</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>Connect via ssh to the Raspberry pi. ssh &lt;username&gt;@@&lt;url_of_your_raspberrypi&gt;</MudText>
<br />
<MudStack Row="true">
   <MudText>curl -fsSL https://get.Docker.com -o get-Docker.sh; sudo sh get-Docker.sh;</MudText>
   <MudFab @onclick="@(() => CopyToClipboard("curl -fsSL https://get.Docker.com -o get-Docker.sh;"))"
           Color="Color.Primary"
           StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ContentCopy"
           Size="Size.Small"
           IconSize="Size.Small" />
</MudStack>
<MudStack Row="true">
   <MudText>sudo sh get-Docker.sh</MudText>
   <MudFab @onclick="@(() => CopyToClipboard("sudo sh get-Docker.sh"))"
           Color="Color.Primary"
           StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ContentCopy"
           Size="Size.Small"
           IconSize="Size.Small" />
</MudStack>
<br />
<br />
<MudText Typo="Typo.h5">Step 2 Copy the source code to the Raspberry Pi</MudText>
<br />
<MudText>If the iotzoo stack is already running, stop and delete it (the volume with the databases is kept).</MudText>
<MudStack Row="true">
   <MudText>docker compose down --rmi local</MudText>
   <MudFab @onclick="@(() => CopyToClipboard("docker compose down --rmi local"))"
           Color="Color.Primary"
           StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ContentCopy"
           Size="Size.Small"
           IconSize="Size.Small" />
</MudStack>

<br />
<MudText>A convinient method is to do this with WinSCP.</MudText>
<br />
<br />
<MudText Typo="Typo.h5">Step 3 Build and start the container</MudText>
<br />
<br />
<MudStack Row="true">
   <MudText>sudo su</MudText>
   <MudFab @onclick="@(() => CopyToClipboard("sudo su"))"
           Color="Color.Primary"
           StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ContentCopy"
           Size="Size.Small"
           IconSize="Size.Small" />
</MudStack>
<br />
<MudText>Switch to the folder where the docker-compose.yml file is located (folder /Server). Enter the following command in this folder:</MudText>
<br />
<MudStack Row="true">
   <MudText>docker compose up -d --build</MudText>
   <MudFab @onclick="@(() => CopyToClipboard("docker compose up -d --build"))"
           Color="Color.Primary"
           StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ContentCopy"
           Size="Size.Small"
           IconSize="Size.Small" />
</MudStack>
<br />
<MudStack Row="true">
   <MudText>docker compose ps</MudText>
   <MudFab @onclick="@(() => CopyToClipboard("docker compose ps"))"
            Color="Color.Primary"
            StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ContentCopy"
            Size="Size.Small"
            IconSize="Size.Small" />
</MudStack>
<br />
<br />
<MudStack Row="true">
   <MudText Typo="Typo.h5">Step 4 Test in Browser</MudText>
</MudStack>
<br />
<MudText>http://&lt;url_of_your_raspberrypi&gt;:8085</MudText>
<br />
<br />
<MudText>Note: The SQLite databases are stored in the Docker volume "iotzoo_databases". They are not lost when a newer version is copied to the Raspberry Pi and started again with "docker compose up -d --build". They are only deleted by "docker compose down -v" or "docker volume rm".</MudText>